Solarized Dark and Solarized Light (src/themes/solarized-*.json)
----------------------------------------------------------------

Files:     src/themes/solarized-dark.json, solarized-dark-adjusted.json, solarized-light.json,
          solarized-light-adjusted.json
Source:    https://github.com/altercation/solarized/blob/master/README.md (palette and roles)
          and
          https://github.com/altercation/solarized/blob/master/vim-colors-solarized/colors/solarized.vim
          (syntax)
Version:   commit 62f656a02f93c5190a8753159e34b385588d5ff3 (the repository has no release)
Licence:  MIT

Mapping:   By the README's roles: dark is base03 background, base02 background highlights,
          base01 comments and secondary content, base0 body text; light swaps to base3, base2,
          base1 and base00. surface and surface-sunken = background, surface-raised and
          selection = background highlights, border, hairline, text-muted, text-disabled,
          syntax-comment and syntax-punctuation (htmlTag) = comments, text = body, accent and
          focus-ring = blue, accent-text = background, hover = comments at 25 % over
          surface-raised, active-line = background highlights (CursorLine) at 50 %,
          active-line-gutter = it composited over surface, error = red, warning = yellow, info
          = cyan, success = green. Syntax from solarized.vim: keyword green (Statement),
          function blue (Identifier), constant and string cyan (Constant), tag blue
          (htmlTagName), attribute base00 / base0 (htmlArg). Upstream has no scrim or shadow
          colour; those are Tyto Dark's and Tyto Light's.
