Tokyo Night and Tokyo Night Light (src/themes/tokyo-night*.json)
----------------------------------------------------------------

Files:     src/themes/tokyo-night.json, tokyo-night-adjusted.json, tokyo-night-light.json,
          tokyo-night-light-adjusted.json
Source:
          https://github.com/enkia/tokyo-night-vscode-theme/blob/master/themes/tokyo-night-color-theme.json
          and tokyo-night-light-color-theme.json
Version:   package.json 1.1.2, commit 7c0f11eaef322f293621ca7befe462214b7ea468
Licence:  MIT

Mapping:   From the VS Code theme's workbench colours and tokenColors. surface =
          editor.background, surface-raised = sideBar.background (tabs, title and status bar
          share it), surface-sunken = input.background, border = input.border, hairline =
          editorGroup.border, text = editor.foreground, text-muted = foreground (the UI's
          text), text-disabled = disabledForeground, accent = tab.activeBorder, accent-text =
          button.foreground, focus-ring = focusBorder, selection = editor.selectionBackground
          composited over surface, hover = list.hoverBackground, error =
          editorError.foreground, warning = editorWarning.foreground, info =
          editorInfo.foreground, success = terminal.ansiGreen, active-line =
          editor.lineHighlightBackground at 50 %, active-line-gutter = it composited over
          surface. Syntax: keyword the 'Keyword' scope, function 'Function Definition',
          constant 'Number, Boolean, Undefined, Null', attribute 'HTML Attributes', string
          'String, Symbols', tag 'Tag', punctuation 'Operator, Misc', comment 'Comment'.
          Upstream has no scrim or shadow colour; those are Tyto Dark's and Tyto Light's. The
          repository's light theme is Tokyo Night Light; it has no 'Day'.
